{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And divinations in their hand.</b> Every kind of divination — so he should not say, 'I have no instruments with me.' Another interpretation: this divination the elders of Midian took in their hand. They said: If he comes with us this time, there is substance to him; and if he puts us off, there is no benefit in him. Therefore when he said to them, 'Lodge here tonight,' they said: there is no hope in him — they left him and went their way, as it says, 'And the princes of Moab stayed with Balaam' — but the elders of Midian went their way (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:08.208392676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}